      "backend": "cuda",
      "hardware_label": "GB10 Grace Blackwell",
      "notes": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 + DFlash speculative decoding on a single DGX Spark (GB10 Blackwell, 128 GiB unified). vLLM 0.19.2rc1 + the DFlash off-by-one patch (without it, drafter reads pre-embedding state and acceptance collapses ~80%\u21923%). Sherlock prose, pp=128, tg=128, c=1, n=29 warm. tokSOut = 102.05 t/s MEDIAN (std 48.74 \u2014 DFlash acceptance varies per token). 2.37\u00d7 over NVFP4 AR baseline (42.98 t/s). peakVramGb=87 at gpu-memory-utilization=0.50 (right-sized from 118 GB at 0.92, no decode regression). KV pool 294K tokens covers the 262K context with 1.12\u00d7 headroom. Tried FP8 KV + alt attention backends to push AR higher \u2014 nothing beat default by >5%, MoE-A3B is bound by expert weights not KV. Repo: github.com/my-other-github-account/spark-bench-reproducers/tree/main/qwen36-35b-a3b-dflash-spark (commit b8776d3, Dockerfile + raw JSONs, reproduces clean-from-scratch). By @banana_baeee.",
      "observed_command": "vllm serve /models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 --served-model-name qwen36-35b-a3b --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --tensor-parallel-size 1 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.50 --max-model-len 262144 --max-num-batched-tokens 4096 --max-num-seqs 1 --trust-remote-code --load-format fastsafetensors --attention-backend flash_attn --enable-prefix-caching --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"dflash\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":15,\"model\":\"/models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-DFlash\"}' --seed 0",
      "run_id": "cmoi65drc000bl104fehrcah8"
